@*
    Spec §6.5: the sidebar's list of Teams, each a root row of the Teams view (no "Teams" header over them: the
    Activity bar already says it). An open Team is a scope list followed by the sections of the selected scope.

    The scope list is the Team itself (its avatar as the chip, linking to /teams/{Team}) and then one row per Project
    in catalog order (the Project's 24px square avatar, linking to /teams/{Team}/projects/{Project}). The Team row is a header
    card with no count; every Project row trails the count of its open Tasks, an em dash when there are none. One row at a time is selected and wears the Selected shape; the Team row is the default. A click selects
    the row and opens its page, and the selection also follows the address: the Team page, its Tasks and its Files
    select the Team row, a Project page and its Tasks and Files select that Project, and a Room selects its Project (or
    the Team row when it has none or its Project is gone). Any other address keeps the last selection of that Team, held
    per circuit. A Project that is no longer in the catalog falls back to the Team row.

    Below the list come the sections of the selected scope, each under a header (a hairline above, a small uppercase
    label and an optional trailing icon button), none of them collapsible:
    PROJECTS (the "+" starts a Project; the Project rows, then, once there is a Project, the quiet "No project" toggle,
    which narrows the sections below to what belongs to no Project), ROOMS (the "+" opens the New chat panel for the Team and the selected
    Project; Team scope lists every Room of the Team, No project the Rooms with no Project or whose Project is gone, a
    Project its own), TASKS (the "+" opens New view; the same Views as TaskViewNav.razor, each linking to
    /teams/{Team}/tasks/{ViewId}, /teams/{Team}/no-project/tasks/{ViewId} or /teams/{Team}/projects/{Project}/tasks/{ViewId};
    Rename and Delete stay on the Tasks view's own rows) and LIBRARY (one Files link to the Library tab of the scope; No
    project links to /teams/{Team}/no-project/files, the Team's folder without its Project folders).

    Copies TaskViewNav.razor's shape: subscribe to ITeamCatalog.Changed, marshal with
    DispatchAsync and unsubscribe in Dispose (the catalog is a singleton, so an undisposed
    subscription would throw on the next publish after this component is torn down), plus the
    row-actions menu - a keyboard-focusable "..." MudIconButton and a right-click on the row, both
    opening the SAME MudMenu instance through an @ref. The counts follow TaskEvents the way the Tasks page does.

    A MudNavGroup title toggles the group and has no Href, so a Team is a link plus a separate chevron rather than a
    nested group.

    With Team set (a Team shortcut in the Activity bar, TeamShortcutBar.razor) it lists that one Team's scope list and
    sections and nothing else: no Team row and no "Show all" over the Teams. Its header card ends in an Unfold More
    button that unfolds every Team inside the card in catalog order (the one shown marked in its own place, so no Team moves with the selection), then "Build a team"; picking a Team folds it, raises TeamChanged
    (MainLayout shows that Team's view as its shortcut tile would) and opens the Team page. Its Rooms section is drawn
    even when empty and splits into "Needs you" and "All" while a Room in the scope waits on the Human. A Team with no
    Rooms, Projects or Task Views shows its header card (the link to the Team page, and the switcher), an empty state,
    the Rooms header (so a first chat can be started) and the Library link in place of the list.

    With IsTeamsView set (the Activity bar's Teams view, MainLayout.razor) it is that same single-Team view, for the last
    Team used (Team) or the catalog's first, with the card's Team list unfolded from the start and after a pick. Neither
    Team nor IsTeamsView set lists every Team, as the Teams view used to. Archived Teams and Projects are listed and restored
    on the Archived page; this nav only archives (the Team row's menu, and the scope rows' menus).
*@

@using System.Globalization
@using System.Text.Json
@using Agency.Huddle.App.Components.Shared.Dialogs
@using Agency.Huddle.App.Library
@using Agency.Huddle.App.NeedsYou
@using Agency.Huddle.App.SecondBrain
@using Agency.Huddle.App.Tabs
@using Agency.Huddle.App.TeamTypes
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@implements IDisposable
@inject IArchiveService Archive
@inject ITeamCatalog Catalog
@inject ITeamDirectory TeamDirectory
@inject RoomEvents Events
@inject ITeamFolders Folders
@inject ViewStore Views
@inject TaskStore Store
@inject TaskEvents TaskSignals
@inject TabService Tabs
@inject IDialogService Dialogs
@inject ISnackbar Snackbar
@inject IOptions<TeamOptions> TeamConfig
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IJSRuntime JS
@inject NeedsYouTracker Tracker
@inject TeamTypeCatalog TeamTypes

<div class="teams-nav-host">
    <MudNavMenu Class="teams-nav">
        @foreach (TeamSummary team in this.ListedTeams())
        {
            bool isExpanded = this.OneTeam is not null || this.IsExpanded(team.Name);
            string? scope = this.SelectedProject(team);
            bool noProject = this.IsNoProject(team, scope);
            @if (this.OneTeam is null)
            {
                @* Keyed by the Team, so its menu is never reused for another Team's row and keeps its own @ref (see menuRefs). *@
                <div class="hover-reveal-row" @key="team.Name"
                     @oncontextmenu="@(e => this.OnRowContextMenuAsync(team.Name, e))"
                     @oncontextmenu:preventDefault="true">
                    <MudIconButton Icon="@(isExpanded ? Icons.Material.Filled.ExpandMore : Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight)"
                                   Size="Size.Small" Class="teams-nav-chevron"
                                   aria-label="@(isExpanded ? $"Collapse {team.Name}" : $"Expand {team.Name}")"
                                   aria-expanded="@(isExpanded ? "true" : "false")"
                                   OnClick="@(() => this.ToggleAsync(team.Name))" />
                    <NavTabLink Href="@($"/teams/{Uri.EscapeDataString(team.Name)}")" TabTitle="@team.Name" Match="NavLinkMatch.Prefix"
                                Class="hover-reveal-link"><TeamAvatar Team="@team.Name" Avatar="team.Avatar" Size="Size.Small" Class="teams-nav-avatar" /><span class="sidebar-row-label" title="@team.Name">@team.Name</span></NavTabLink>
                    @* Meta never takes the row's text: the member count trails the name, and its tooltip says what it counts. *@
                    <span class="sidebar-row-meta" title="@(team.HasMembers ? Plural.Of(team.Members.Count, "member", "members") : "No members")">@team.Members.Count</span>
                    <MudMenu @ref="@this.menuRefs[team.Name]" Class="hover-reveal-menu" Dense="true">
                        @* ActivatorContent replaces MudMenu's own built-in activator entirely, so
                           MudMenu does not wire a click listener around it automatically - the
                           supplied MenuContext.ToggleAsync is how custom activator content opens
                           the menu (TaskViewNav.razor's and RoomList.razor's own precedent). *@
                        <ActivatorContent Context="menuContext">
                            @* No hover tooltip (it would stay up over the first item); the label names the Team. *@
                            <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.MoreVert" Size="Size.Small"
                                           aria-label="@MenuDialogs.ActivatorLabel(team.Name)" Class="hover-reveal-menu-button"
                                           OnClick="menuContext.ToggleAsync" />
                        </ActivatorContent>
                        <ChildContent>
                            <MudMenuItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Add" OnClick="@(() => this.ToggleNewChat(team.Name))">New chat</MudMenuItem>
                            @if (this.ProjectsAllowed)
                            {
                                <MudMenuItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Add" OnClick="@(() => this.NewProjectAsync(team.Name, this.menuRefs.GetValueOrDefault(team.Name)))">New project…</MudMenuItem>
                            }
                            <MudMenuItem Icon="@ArchiveIcon" Class="teams-nav-archive-team"
                                         OnClick="@(() => this.ArchiveTeamAsync(team.Name, this.menuRefs.GetValueOrDefault(team.Name)))">Archive team…</MudMenuItem>
                        </ChildContent>
                    </MudMenu>
                </div>
                @* The Team's own panel sits under its row, unless its Rooms section is on screen to hold it. *@
                @if (this.IsNewChatOpen(team.Name, null) && !(isExpanded && scope is null))
                {
                    <NewChat Team="@team.Name" OnStarted="this.EndNewChat" OnClosed="this.EndNewChat" />
                }
            }
            @if (isExpanded)
            {
                IReadOnlyList<Room> allRooms = this.RoomsOf(team);
                @if (this.OneTeam is not null && allRooms.Count == 0 && team.Projects.Count == 0 && !this.ShowsTasksFolder)
                {
                    @* The header card stays, so its switcher still reaches the other Teams. *@
                    <div class="teams-nav-scope-block teams-nav-scopes" data-team="@team.Name">
                        @this.TeamCard(team, scope is null, this.OpenTaskCounts(team.Name))
                    </div>
                    <EmptyState Title="@($"Nothing in {team.Name} yet")" Text="Its Rooms, Projects and Task Views will be listed here." />
                    @* Nothing to list yet, but the Human can still start a chat or a Project here and reach the Team's Files. *@
                    <div class="teams-nav-scope-block" data-team="@team.Name">
                        @if (this.ProjectsAllowed)
                        {
                            <div class="teams-nav-section teams-nav-section-projects" data-section="projects">
                                @SectionHeader("Projects", this.StartProjectButton(team.Name))
                            </div>
                        }
                        @this.RoomsSection(team, null, allRooms, noProject: false)
                        @this.LibrarySection(team.Name, null)
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="teams-nav-scope-block" data-team="@team.Name">
                        @this.ScopeList(team, scope, noProject)
                        @this.RoomsSection(team, scope, allRooms, noProject)
                        @if (this.ShowsTasksFolder)
                        {
                            @this.TasksSection(team.Name, scope, noProject)
                        }
                        @this.LibrarySection(team.Name, scope, noProject)
                    </div>
                }
            }
        }
        @if (this.OneTeam is null)
        {
            <ShowAllRow Total="this.Catalog.Teams.Count" Expanded="this.showAllTeams" OnToggle="this.ToggleShowAllTeams" />
            <NavTabLink Href="/teams/build" TabTitle="Build a team" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Add" Class="nav-action-link">Build a team</NavTabLink>
        }
    </MudNavMenu>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The one Team to list the scope list and sections of, from its Activity bar shortcut, or <see langword="null"/> for every Team.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Team { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether this is the Activity bar's Teams view: it shows one Team as a shortcut does (<see cref="Team"/>, the last
    /// one used, or the catalog's first while there is none or it is gone), with the header card's Team list unfolded
    /// by default and kept unfolded after a pick. Archived Teams are listed on the Archived page, not here.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool IsTeamsView { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Raised with the shortcut's <see cref="Team"/> when the catalog no longer lists it (it was archived or removed), so the
    /// layout can stop showing this view, which would be empty. Never raised in the Teams view, which falls back to another Team.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> TeamGone { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The one Team this nav shows, or <see langword="null"/> for every Team: <see cref="Team"/>, or in the Teams view the last used Team while the catalog still lists it, else the catalog's first.</summary>
    private string? OneTeam => !this.IsTeamsView
        ? this.Team
        : this.Catalog.Teams.FirstOrDefault(candidate => string.Equals(candidate.Name, this.Team, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))?.Name
            ?? this.Catalog.Teams.FirstOrDefault()?.Name;

    /// <summary>Raised with the Team picked in the header card's switcher, so the layout shows that Team's view instead.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string?> TeamChanged { get; set; }

    private bool showAllTeams;

    /// <summary>Folder keys (see <see cref="FolderKey"/>) whose list the Human opened with "Show all".</summary>
    private readonly HashSet<string> showAllRows = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
    private readonly Dictionary<string, MudMenu> menuRefs = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    private const string ExpandedKey = "teamsNav:expanded";

    /// <summary>Lower-cased names of the Teams the user opened (stored under <c>teamsNav:expanded</c>); a Team not in it is collapsed unless the route is inside it.</summary>
    private readonly HashSet<string> opened = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);

    /// <summary>The key parts of the lists a scope shows, after a control character that keeps them apart from any Team name. The Projects list, the Rooms section and the Tasks section each append the scope to theirs.</summary>
    private const string ProjectFolder = "\u0001project";
    private const string RoomsFolder = "\u0001rooms";
    private const string TasksFolder = "\u0001tasks";

    /// <summary>The two folders inside a shortcut's Rooms section while a Room in the scope waits on the Human.</summary>
    private const string NeedsYouFolder = RoomsFolder + "\u0001needs-you";
    private const string AllFolder = RoomsFolder + "\u0001all";

    /// <summary>The ids of the Rooms waiting on the Human, as the tracker holds them.</summary>
    private HashSet<string> waitingIds = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);

    private bool IsWaiting(Room room) => this.waitingIds.Contains(room.Id);

    /// <summary>
    /// The scope list: the Team's own row, then under a PROJECTS header a row per Project (cut to the first few until "Show all",
    /// always keeping the selected one), then, once there is a Project, the quiet "No project" row. The header's "+" starts a Project.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team whose scopes to list.</param>
    /// <param name="selected">The selected Project, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team row or No project.</param>
    /// <param name="noProject">Whether "No project" is the selected scope.</param>
    private RenderFragment ScopeList(TeamSummary team, string? selected, bool noProject)
    {
        IReadOnlyDictionary<string, int> counts = this.OpenTaskCounts(team.Name);
        string listKey = FolderKey(team.Name, ProjectFolder);
        return @<div class="teams-nav-scopes">
            @this.TeamCard(team, selected is null && !noProject, counts)
            @if (this.ProjectsAllowed || team.Projects.Count > 0)
            {
                <div class="teams-nav-section teams-nav-section-projects" data-section="projects">
                    @SectionHeader("Projects", this.ProjectsAllowed ? this.StartProjectButton(team.Name) : null)
                    @foreach (string project in SidebarRows.Visible(team.Projects, this.showAllRows.Contains(listKey), candidate => string.Equals(candidate, selected, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)))
                    {
                        @this.ScopeRow(team, project, string.Equals(project, selected, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase), counts)
                    }
                    <ShowAllRow Total="team.Projects.Count" Expanded="this.showAllRows.Contains(listKey)" OnToggle="@(() => this.ToggleShowAllRows(listKey))" />
                    @if (team.Projects.Count > 0)
                    {
                        @this.NoProjectRow(team.Name, noProject, counts)
                    }
                </div>
            }
        </div>;
    }

    /// <summary>The PROJECTS header's "+" (tooltip "Start a project"), the same button as the ROOMS and TASKS headers' "+": it opens the New project prompt.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team the Project is started in.</param>
    private RenderFragment StartProjectButton(string team) =>
        @<MudTooltip Text="Start a project">
            <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Add" Size="Size.Small" Class="teams-nav-section-add teams-nav-start-project"
                           aria-label="Start a project" OnClick="@(() => this.NewProjectAsync(team, null))" />
        </MudTooltip>;

    /// <summary>
    /// The quiet "No project" row: selecting it narrows the sections below to the Team's Rooms and Tasks that belong to no Project.
    /// It has no page of its own, so it is a toggle button rather than a link; a second click returns to the Team row.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team.</param>
    /// <param name="selected">Whether No project is the selected scope.</param>
    /// <param name="counts">The Team's open Task counts (see <see cref="OpenTaskCounts"/>); the Team-level ones are under the empty key.</param>
    private RenderFragment NoProjectRow(string team, bool selected, IReadOnlyDictionary<string, int> counts)
    {
        int open = counts.GetValueOrDefault(string.Empty);
        return @<button type="button" class="@(selected ? "teams-nav-switcher-item teams-nav-no-project selected-shape" : "teams-nav-switcher-item teams-nav-no-project")"
                        aria-pressed="@(selected ? "true" : "false")" title="Rooms, Tasks and files that belong to no project"
                        @onclick="@(() => this.ToggleNoProject(team))">
            <span class="sidebar-row-label">@Tasks.NoProjectLabel</span>
            @if (this.TeamConfig.Value.Tasks.Enabled)
            {
                <span class="sidebar-row-meta teams-nav-scope-count" title="@(open == 0 ? "No open tasks" : Plural.Of(open, "open task", "open tasks"))">@(open == 0 ? "—" : open.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture))</span>
            }
        </button>;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The Team's header card: one bordered container holding the Team's own scope row and, while the switcher is
    /// unfolded under a Team shortcut, the other Teams below it, each drawn as the Team row is.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team.</param>
    /// <param name="selected">Whether the Team row is the selected scope.</param>
    /// <param name="counts">The Team's open Task counts (see <see cref="OpenTaskCounts"/>).</param>
    private RenderFragment TeamCard(TeamSummary team, bool selected, IReadOnlyDictionary<string, int> counts)
    {
        bool open = this.OneTeam is not null && this.switcherOpen;
        return @<div class="@(open ? "teams-nav-team-card teams-nav-team-card-open" : "teams-nav-team-card")">
            @this.ScopeRow(team, null, selected, counts)
            @if (open)
            {
                @this.TeamSwitcherList(team.Name)
            }
        </div>;
    }
    /// <summary>One scope row: its chip, its name and the count of open Tasks, as one link to the scope's page.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The row's Team.</param>
    /// <param name="project">The row's Project, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team's own row.</param>
    /// <param name="selected">Whether this is the selected scope.</param>
    /// <param name="counts">The Team's open Task counts (see <see cref="OpenTaskCounts"/>).</param>
    private RenderFragment ScopeRow(TeamSummary team, string? project, bool selected, IReadOnlyDictionary<string, int> counts)
    {
        string label = project ?? team.Name;
        string href = ScopeHref(team.Name, project);
        string key = project ?? string.Empty;
        int open = counts.GetValueOrDefault(key);
        string rowClass = (project is null ? "teams-nav-scope-row teams-nav-scope-header" : "teams-nav-scope-row") + (selected ? " selected-shape" : string.Empty);
        string kind = project is null ? "team" : "project";
        return @<div class="@rowClass" @key="key" data-scope="@kind">
            @* A plain link, not a NavLink: the selected look is the row's own, so NavLink's active class never doubles it. *@
            <a class="teams-nav-scope-link" href="@href" title="@label" aria-current="@(selected ? "true" : null)"
               @onclick="@(() => this.OnScopeClick(team.Name, project, href, label))"
               @ondblclick="@(() => this.KeepScopeTab(href))">
                @if (project is null)
                {
                    <TeamAvatar Team="@team.Name" Avatar="team.Avatar" Size="Size.Medium" Class="teams-nav-scope-avatar" />
                    <span class="teams-nav-scope-text">
                        <span class="sidebar-row-label teams-nav-scope-label">@label</span>
                        <span class="teams-nav-scope-subtitle">@this.TeamSubtitle(team)</span>
                    </span>
                }
                else
                {
                    <ProjectAvatar Project="@project" Avatar="team.ProjectAvatar(project)" Class="teams-nav-scope-avatar teams-nav-project-avatar" />
                    <span class="sidebar-row-label teams-nav-scope-label">@label</span>
                }
                @if (project is not null && this.TeamConfig.Value.Tasks.Enabled)
                {
                    <span class="sidebar-row-meta teams-nav-scope-count" title="@(open == 0 ? "No open tasks" : Plural.Of(open, "open task", "open tasks"))">@(open == 0 ? "—" : open.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture))</span>
                }
            </a>
            @* The Team's own row in a one-Team view, and every Project row, carry an Archive menu; in the list of every
               Team the Team row above holds its Archive, so its header card here does not repeat it. *@
            @if (project is not null || this.OneTeam is not null)
            {
                @this.ScopeMenu(team.Name, project)
            }
            @if (project is null && this.OneTeam is not null)
            {
                @this.TeamSwitcher()
            }
        </div>;
    }

    /// <summary>The icon of every Archive action, the one the Team page's and the Project page's Archive buttons use. The Archived page and its Activity bar button use the Archive box instead, for the place rather than the act.</summary>
    private const string ArchiveIcon = Icons.Material.Outlined.Inventory2;

    /// <summary>
    /// The scope rows' menus, by <see cref="ScopeMenuKey"/>, so an item that opens a dialog closes its menu first. Never cleared:
    /// a ref is set only when its menu is created, so clearing would lose the refs of menus that stay on screen; a gone row's entry is
    /// never looked up again.
    /// </summary>
    private readonly Dictionary<string, MudMenu> scopeMenuRefs = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    /// <summary>The key of a scope row's menu: the Team, then the Project after a control character no name holds.</summary>
    private static string ScopeMenuKey(string team, string? project) => team + "\u0001" + project;

    /// <summary>
    /// A scope row's "..." menu, shown while the row is hovered or focused (sidebar.css): Archive team… on the Team's row,
    /// Archive project on a Project's. It sits beside the row's link, not inside it, so opening it never opens the page.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="team">The row's Team.</param>
    /// <param name="project">The row's Project, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team's own row.</param>
    private RenderFragment ScopeMenu(string team, string? project)
    {
        string key = ScopeMenuKey(team, project);
        string label = project ?? team;
        // Keyed by Team and Project: Blazor sets @ref only when it creates the instance, so a menu reused for another Team's
        // header (the row keeps its place when the Team changes) would leave this key without a ref and the menu could not close first.
        RenderFragment menu = @<MudMenu @key="key" @ref="@this.scopeMenuRefs[key]" Class="teams-nav-scope-menu" Dense="true">
            <ActivatorContent Context="menuContext">
                <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.MoreVert" Size="Size.Small" Class="teams-nav-scope-menu-button"
                               aria-label="@MenuDialogs.ActivatorLabel(label)" OnClick="menuContext.ToggleAsync" />
            </ActivatorContent>
            <ChildContent>
                @if (project is null)
                {
                    <MudMenuItem Icon="@ArchiveIcon" Class="teams-nav-archive-team"
                                 OnClick="@(() => this.ArchiveTeamAsync(team, this.scopeMenuRefs.GetValueOrDefault(key)))">Archive team…</MudMenuItem>
                }
                else
                {
                    <MudMenuItem Icon="@ArchiveIcon" Class="teams-nav-archive-project"
                                 OnClick="@(() => this.ArchiveProjectAsync(team, project))">Archive project</MudMenuItem>
                }
            </ChildContent>
        </MudMenu>;
        return menu;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Asks T16's question and archives the Team (see <see cref="TeamArchiveActions"/>). Once archived, its Tabs close here
    /// rather than waiting for TabSync, which leaves them open when the last Team goes; the page follows the Tab that is
    /// active afterwards, or goes Home when none is left. The catalog change then drops the Team's rows.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team whose menu was used.</param>
    /// <param name="menu">That menu, closed before the confirm opens.</param>
    private async Task ArchiveTeamAsync(string team, MudMenu? menu)
    {
        if (!await TeamArchiveActions.ArchiveTeamAsync(this.Archive, this.Dialogs, this.Snackbar, team, menu))
        {
            return;
        }

        string? activeBefore = this.Tabs.Active?.Id;
        TabReconciler.CloseTeamTabs(this.Tabs, team);
        if (activeBefore is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        if (this.Tabs.Active is not { } now)
        {
            this.Navigation.NavigateTo("/");
        }
        else if (!string.Equals(now.Id, activeBefore, StringComparison.Ordinal))
        {
            this.Navigation.NavigateTo(now.Url);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Archives the Project with no confirmation, as the Project page's own Archive does; the selection falls back to the Team row once the catalog drops it.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Project's Team.</param>
    /// <param name="project">The Project.</param>
    private async Task ArchiveProjectAsync(string team, string project)
    {
        _ = await TeamArchiveActions.ArchiveProjectAsync(this.Archive, this.Snackbar, team, project);
    }

    /// <summary>Whether the header card's Team list is unfolded under it: folded at first under a shortcut, unfolded at first in the Teams view.</summary>
    private bool switcherOpen;

    /// <summary>
    /// The header card's Unfold More button in a Team shortcut's view: it unfolds the list of the other Teams under the
    /// card (see <see cref="TeamSwitcherList"/>) and folds it again. It sits beside the card's link, not inside it, so a
    /// click on it never opens the Team page.
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment TeamSwitcher() =>
        @<MudIconButton Icon="@(this.switcherOpen ? Icons.Material.Filled.UnfoldLess : Icons.Material.Filled.UnfoldMore)" Size="Size.Small"
                        Class="teams-nav-switcher-button" aria-label="Switch team" title="Switch team"
                        aria-expanded="@(this.switcherOpen ? "true" : "false")" OnClick="this.ToggleSwitcher" />;

    /// <summary>
    /// Every Team in catalog order, unfolded under the header card while <see cref="switcherOpen"/>, then "Build a team".
    /// The Team shown stays in its own place, marked, so a Team's position never moves with the selection; picking
    /// another shows its view, as its shortcut tile would.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="current">The Team the view shows, marked in the list.</param>
    private RenderFragment TeamSwitcherList(string current) =>
        @<div class="teams-nav-switcher-list" role="list" aria-label="Teams">
            @foreach (TeamSummary other in this.Catalog.Teams)
            {
                string name = other.Name;
                bool isCurrent = string.Equals(name, current, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
                <button type="button" role="listitem" class="@(isCurrent ? "teams-nav-switcher-item selected-shape" : "teams-nav-switcher-item")"
                        @key="name" title="@name" aria-current="@(isCurrent ? "true" : null)"
                        @onclick="@(() => this.SwitchTeamAsync(name))">
                    <TeamAvatar Team="@name" Avatar="other.Avatar" Size="Size.Medium" Class="teams-nav-scope-avatar" />
                    <span class="teams-nav-scope-text">
                        <span class="sidebar-row-label teams-nav-scope-label">@name</span>
                        <span class="teams-nav-scope-subtitle">@this.TeamSubtitle(other)</span>
                    </span>
                </button>
            }
            <button type="button" role="listitem" class="teams-nav-switcher-item teams-nav-switcher-build" @onclick="this.BuildTeam">
                <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Add" Size="Size.Small" Class="teams-nav-switcher-build-icon" />
                <span class="sidebar-row-label">Build a team</span>
            </button>
        </div>;

    private void ToggleSwitcher() => this.switcherOpen = !this.switcherOpen;

    /// <summary>Opens the Build a team page from the switcher, as its old sidebar link did (in the preview Tab), and folds the list under a shortcut.</summary>
    private void BuildTeam()
    {
        const string href = "/teams/build";
        this.switcherOpen = this.IsTeamsView;
        _ = this.Tabs.Open(href, "Build a team");
        this.Navigation.NavigateTo(href);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Folds the list, asks the layout to show <paramref name="team"/>'s view and opens the Team's page as a click on its
    /// card does: offered to the Tabs first, so it replaces the unpinned preview Tab rather than adding one, then navigated to.
    /// Picking the Team already shown changes nothing more.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team picked in the switcher.</param>
    private async Task SwitchTeamAsync(string team)
    {
        this.switcherOpen = this.IsTeamsView;
        if (string.Equals(team, this.OneTeam, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
        {
            return;
        }

        await this.TeamChanged.InvokeAsync(team);
        string href = ScopeHref(team, null);
        this.SelectScope(team, null);
        _ = this.Tabs.Open(href, team);
        this.Navigation.NavigateTo(href);
    }

    /// <summary>The Team header card's second line: the Team type's display name and the member count ("Research Team · 8 members"), or just the count when the Team has no type.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team.</param>
    private string TeamSubtitle(TeamSummary team)
    {
        string members = Plural.Of(team.Members.Count, "member", "members");
        if (team.TeamType is not { } type)
        {
            return members;
        }

        string name = string.Equals(type.Id, BlankTeamType.Id, StringComparison.Ordinal)
            ? BlankTeamType.Manifest.DisplayName
            : this.TeamTypes.Find(type.Id)?.DisplayName ?? type.Id;
        return $"{name} · {members}";
    }

    /// <summary>A section's header: a hairline above, the small uppercase label and, when given, a trailing control.</summary>
    /// <param name="title">The label.</param>
    /// <param name="trailing">The control at the end of the header, or <see langword="null"/> for none.</param>
    private static RenderFragment SectionHeader(string title, RenderFragment? trailing = null) =>
        @<div class="teams-nav-section-header">
            <span class="teams-nav-section-title">@title</span>
            @trailing
        </div>;

    /// <summary>The ROOMS section of a scope: the header with its "+", the New chat panel while open, then the scope's Rooms.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team.</param>
    /// <param name="project">The selected Project, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team scope or No project.</param>
    /// <param name="allRooms">Every Room listed under the Team.</param>
    /// <param name="noProject">Whether No project is the selected scope: only the Rooms with no Project (or whose Project is gone); the Team scope lists every Room.</param>
    private RenderFragment RoomsSection(TeamSummary team, string? project, IReadOnlyList<Room> allRooms, bool noProject)
    {
        List<Room> rooms = project is null && !noProject ? [.. allRooms] : [.. ScopeRooms(team, allRooms, project)];
        string scopeKey = ScopeFolderSuffix(project, noProject);
        string roomsKey = FolderKey(team.Name, RoomsFolder + scopeKey);
        string newChatLabel = $"New chat in {project ?? team.Name}";
        RenderFragment add = @<MudTooltip Text="@newChatLabel">
            <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Add" Size="Size.Small" Class="teams-nav-section-add"
                           aria-label="@newChatLabel"
                           OnClick="@(() => this.ToggleNewChat(team.Name, project))" />
        </MudTooltip>;
        return @<div class="teams-nav-section teams-nav-section-rooms" data-section="rooms">
            @SectionHeader("Rooms", add)
            @if (this.IsNewChatOpen(team.Name, project))
            {
                <NewChat Team="@team.Name" Project="@project" OnStarted="this.EndNewChat" OnClosed="this.EndNewChat" />
            }
            @if (this.OneTeam is null)
            {
                @foreach (Room room in SidebarRows.Visible(rooms, this.showAllRows.Contains(roomsKey), this.IsActiveRoom))
                {
                    <RoomNavRow @key="room.Id" Room="room" Members="this.MembersOf(room)" Class="nav-team-room-link" OnError="this.OnRoomError" />
                }
                <ShowAllRow Total="rooms.Count" Expanded="this.showAllRows.Contains(roomsKey)" OnToggle="@(() => this.ToggleShowAllRows(roomsKey))" />
            }
            else
            {
                @this.ShortcutRooms(team.Name, scopeKey, rooms)
            }
        </div>;
    }

    /// <summary>A shortcut's Rooms: the Chats view's All grouping for one scope, the Rooms waiting on the Human in a "Needs you" folder and the rest in "All", every Room listed with no "Show all". With nothing waiting there is nothing to split, so the Rooms are listed flat.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The shortcut's Team.</param>
    /// <param name="scopeKey">The selected scope's part of the folder keys (see <see cref="ScopeFolderSuffix"/>).</param>
    /// <param name="rooms">The scope's Rooms.</param>
    private RenderFragment ShortcutRooms(string team, string scopeKey, List<Room> rooms)
    {
        List<Room> waiting = [.. rooms.Where(this.IsWaiting)];
        string needsYouKey = FolderKey(team, NeedsYouFolder + scopeKey);
        string allKey = FolderKey(team, AllFolder + scopeKey);
        return @<text>
            @if (waiting.Count > 0)
            {
                <MudNavGroup Class="teams-nav-subfolder room-folder-needs-you" Title="Needs you" Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.NotificationsActive"
                             Expanded="this.IsFolderOpen(needsYouKey)" ExpandedChanged="@(open => this.SetFolderOpen(needsYouKey, open))">
                    @foreach (Room room in waiting)
                    {
                        <RoomNavRow @key="room.Id" Room="room" Members="this.MembersOf(room)" Class="nav-team-room-link" OnError="this.OnRoomError" />
                    }
                </MudNavGroup>
                <MudNavGroup Class="teams-nav-subfolder teams-nav-all" Title="All" Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.Folder"
                             Expanded="this.IsFolderOpen(allKey)" ExpandedChanged="@(open => this.SetFolderOpen(allKey, open))">
                    @foreach (Room room in rooms.Where(room => !this.IsWaiting(room)))
                    {
                        <RoomNavRow @key="room.Id" Room="room" Members="this.MembersOf(room)" Class="nav-team-room-link" OnError="this.OnRoomError" />
                    }
                </MudNavGroup>
            }
            else
            {
                @foreach (Room room in rooms)
                {
                    <RoomNavRow @key="room.Id" Room="room" Members="this.MembersOf(room)" Class="nav-team-room-link" OnError="this.OnRoomError" />
                }
            }
        </text>;
    }

    /// <summary>The TASKS section: every View, each linking to the Tasks page narrowed to the Team, or to the Team's Project when <paramref name="project"/> is set.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team the Views are narrowed to.</param>
    /// <param name="project">The Project they are narrowed to, or <see langword="null"/> for every Task of the Team (or, with <paramref name="noProject"/>, its Tasks that have no Project).</param>
    /// <param name="noProject">Whether No project is the selected scope.</param>
    private RenderFragment TasksSection(string team, string? project, bool noProject)
    {
        string tasksKey = FolderKey(team, TasksFolder + ScopeFolderSuffix(project, noProject));
        string? titleScope = noProject ? Tasks.NoProjectLabel : project;
        RenderFragment add = @<MudTooltip Text="New task view">
            <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Add" Size="Size.Small" Class="teams-nav-section-add teams-nav-new-view"
                           aria-label="New task view" OnClick="this.NewTaskView" />
        </MudTooltip>;
        return @<div class="teams-nav-section teams-nav-section-tasks" data-section="tasks">
            @SectionHeader("Tasks", add)
            @foreach (TaskView view in SidebarRows.Visible(this.Views.Views, this.showAllRows.Contains(tasksKey), candidate => this.IsActiveView(team, project, noProject, candidate)))
            {
                <NavTabLink @key="view.Id" Href="@ViewHref(team, project, noProject, view.Id)"
                            TabTitle="@Tasks.TeamViewTitle(team, view.Name, titleScope)"
                            Icon="@(view.Kind == ViewKind.Kanban ? Icons.Material.Outlined.ViewKanban : Icons.Material.Outlined.ViewList)"
                            Class="nav-team-view-link"><span class="sidebar-row-label" title="@view.Name">@view.Name</span></NavTabLink>
            }
            <ShowAllRow Total="this.Views.Views.Count" Expanded="this.showAllRows.Contains(tasksKey)" OnToggle="@(() => this.ToggleShowAllRows(tasksKey))" />
        </div>;
    }

    /// <summary>The LIBRARY section: one Files link to the Library of the Team, of its Project, or of No project (the Team's files outside every Project folder); nothing while the Library is off.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team.</param>
    /// <param name="project">The Project, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team's own Library or No project's.</param>
    /// <param name="noProject">Whether No project is the selected scope.</param>
    private RenderFragment LibrarySection(string team, string? project, bool noProject = false)
    {
        if (!this.TeamConfig.Value.Library.Enabled)
        {
            return static _ => { };
        }

        string teamHref = $"/teams/{Uri.EscapeDataString(team)}";
        string href = project is not null ? $"{teamHref}/projects/{Uri.EscapeDataString(project)}/files" : $"{teamHref}/files";
        if (project is null && noProject)
        {
            href = $"{teamHref}/{NoProjectSegment}/files";
        }

        string title = project ?? (noProject ? Tasks.NoProjectLabel : team);
        return @<div class="teams-nav-section teams-nav-section-library" data-section="library">
            @SectionHeader("Library")
            <NavTabLink Href="@href" TabTitle="@title" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.LibraryBooks"
                        Class="teams-nav-library-link"><span class="sidebar-row-label">Files</span></NavTabLink>
        </div>;
    }

    /// <summary>Folder keys of the folders the Human closed. Every folder starts open, and the choice lasts for this circuit only.</summary>
    private readonly HashSet<string> closedFolders = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    /// <summary>The lower-cased, unescaped Team of the current route, or <see langword="null"/> outside <c>/teams/{Team}</c>.</summary>
    private string? routeTeam;

    /// <summary>Whether the route's Team is forced open: set by every navigation, cleared when the chevron collapses that Team.</summary>
    private bool routeOpen;

    /// <summary>Each Team's selected scope for this circuit: the Project's name as the address or Room spelled it, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team row. Keyed by Team name ignoring case; a Team not in it has the Team row selected.</summary>
    private readonly Dictionary<string, string?> selections = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    private EventHandler<LocationChangedEventArgs>? locationChanged;

    /// <summary>Each Team's Rooms to list under it: its Team Room first (when not archived), then its other unarchived scoped Rooms, oldest first. Keyed by Team name ignoring case.</summary>
    private readonly Dictionary<string, IReadOnlyList<Room>> roomsByTeam = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
    private IReadOnlyDictionary<string, IReadOnlyList<User>> membersByRoom = new Dictionary<string, IReadOnlyList<User>>(StringComparer.Ordinal);

    /// <summary>The Team whose New chat panel is open, or <see langword="null"/>.</summary>
    private string? newChatTeam;

    /// <summary>The Project the open New chat panel is for, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team's own panel.</summary>
    private string? newChatProject;

    /// <summary>Counts the Room loads started; a load that finds a higher number than its own has been overtaken and drops its result.</summary>
    private int loadVersion;

    /// <summary>Subscribes to <see cref="ITeamCatalog.Changed"/>, <see cref="RoomEvents.RoomsChanged"/>, <see cref="ViewStore.ViewsChanged"/>, <see cref="TaskEvents"/> and navigation, reads the route's Team and loads each Team's Rooms.</summary>
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        this.switcherOpen = this.IsTeamsView;
        this.Catalog.Changed += this.OnCatalogChanged;
        this.Events.RoomsChanged += this.OnRoomsChanged;
        this.Views.ViewsChanged += this.OnViewsChanged;
        this.Tracker.Changed += this.OnTrackerChanged;
        this.TaskSignals.TaskChanged += this.OnTaskChanged;
        this.TaskSignals.TasksReloaded += this.OnTasksReloaded;
        this.locationChanged = (_, _) => _ = RendererDispatch.RunAsync(this.InvokeAsync, () =>
        {
            this.UpdateRoute();
            this.StateHasChanged();
            return Task.CompletedTask;
        });
        this.Navigation.LocationChanged += this.locationChanged;
        await this.LoadRoomsAsync();
        this.UpdateRoute();
    }

    /// <summary>Loads the remembered collapsed Teams once, after the first render.</summary>
    /// <param name="firstRender">Whether this is the component's first render.</param>
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (!firstRender)
        {
            return;
        }

        try
        {
            string? stored = await BrowserStorage.TryGetAsync(this.JS, ExpandedKey);
            if (stored is null)
            {
                return;
            }

            string?[]? names = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<string?[]>(stored);
            if (names is null)
            {
                return;
            }

            foreach (string? name in names)
            {
                if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(name))
                {
                    this.opened.Add(name.ToLowerInvariant());
                }
            }

            this.StateHasChanged();
        }
        catch (JsonException)
        {
            // Stored text may be stale or hand-edited and not a JSON array of strings: every Team stays collapsed.
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Unsubscribes from <see cref="ITeamCatalog.Changed"/>, <see cref="RoomEvents.RoomsChanged"/>, <see cref="ViewStore.ViewsChanged"/>, <see cref="TaskEvents"/> and navigation.</summary>
    public void Dispose()
    {
        this.Catalog.Changed -= this.OnCatalogChanged;
        this.Events.RoomsChanged -= this.OnRoomsChanged;
        this.Views.ViewsChanged -= this.OnViewsChanged;
        this.Tracker.Changed -= this.OnTrackerChanged;
        this.TaskSignals.TaskChanged -= this.OnTaskChanged;
        this.TaskSignals.TasksReloaded -= this.OnTasksReloaded;
        if (this.locationChanged is not null)
        {
            this.Navigation.LocationChanged -= this.locationChanged;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>A Team is expanded when it is the route's Team (and the chevron has not collapsed it since the last navigation) or the Human opened it.</summary>
    private bool IsExpanded(string team)
    {
        string key = team.ToLowerInvariant();
        return (this.routeOpen && string.Equals(key, this.routeTeam, StringComparison.Ordinal)) || this.opened.Contains(key);
    }

    /// <summary>The Teams to list: the catalog's rows (cut to the first few until "Show all"), or just <see cref="Team"/> when it is set.</summary>
    private IEnumerable<TeamSummary> ListedTeams() => this.OneTeam is { } only
        ? this.Catalog.Teams.Where(team => string.Equals(team.Name, only, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
        : SidebarRows.Visible(this.Catalog.Teams, this.showAllTeams, this.IsRouteTeam);

    /// <summary>Whether a Team's Tasks section is drawn: Tasks is on and there is a View to list.</summary>
    private bool ShowsTasksFolder => this.TeamConfig.Value.Tasks.Enabled && this.Views.Views.Count > 0;

    private bool IsRouteTeam(TeamSummary team) => string.Equals(team.Name, this.routeTeam, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    private bool IsActiveRoom(Room room) =>
        string.Equals(room.Id, SidebarRows.RoomId(SidebarRows.CurrentPath(this.Navigation)), StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    /// <summary>The address of <paramref name="team"/>'s page, or of its <paramref name="project"/>'s page.</summary>
    private static string ScopeHref(string team, string? project) => project is null
        ? $"/teams/{Uri.EscapeDataString(team)}"
        : $"/teams/{Uri.EscapeDataString(team)}/projects/{Uri.EscapeDataString(project)}";

    /// <summary>
    /// The address of <paramref name="viewId"/> narrowed to <paramref name="team"/> (the Tasks page's <c>/teams/{Team}/tasks/{ViewId}</c> route),
    /// to its Tasks with no Project (<c>/teams/{Team}/no-project/tasks/{ViewId}</c>), or to its <paramref name="project"/>
    /// (<c>/teams/{Team}/projects/{Project}/tasks/{ViewId}</c>).
    /// </summary>
    private static string ViewHref(string team, string? project, bool noProject, string viewId)
    {
        string teamHref = $"/teams/{Uri.EscapeDataString(team)}";
        string view = Uri.EscapeDataString(viewId);
        if (project is not null)
        {
            return $"{teamHref}/projects/{Uri.EscapeDataString(project)}/tasks/{view}";
        }

        return noProject ? $"{teamHref}/{NoProjectSegment}/tasks/{view}" : $"{teamHref}/tasks/{view}";
    }

    private bool IsActiveView(string team, string? project, bool noProject, TaskView view) =>
        string.Equals("/" + SidebarRows.CurrentPath(this.Navigation), ViewHref(team, project, noProject, view.Id), StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    /// <summary>The address segment of the No project scope's Task Views (<c>/teams/{Team}/no-project/tasks/{ViewId}</c>).</summary>
    private const string NoProjectSegment = "no-project";

    /// <summary>The selected scope's part of a folder key: the Project, a control-character marker for No project, or nothing for the Team scope.</summary>
    private static string ScopeFolderSuffix(string? project, bool noProject) => project ?? (noProject ? "\u0001none" : string.Empty);

    /// <summary>Teams whose selected scope is No project (their entry in <see cref="selections"/> is then <see langword="null"/>).</summary>
    private readonly HashSet<string> noProjectTeams = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    /// <summary>Whether No project is <paramref name="team"/>'s selected scope: chosen, and the Team still has a Project for it to differ from the Team row.</summary>
    private bool IsNoProject(TeamSummary team, string? scope) =>
        scope is null && team.Projects.Count > 0 && this.noProjectTeams.Contains(team.Name);

    /// <summary>A click on "No project" selects it, or returns to the Team row when it is already selected; a New chat panel left open closes.</summary>
    private void ToggleNoProject(string team)
    {
        bool wasSelected = this.selections.GetValueOrDefault(team) is null && this.noProjectTeams.Contains(team);
        this.SelectScope(team, null);
        if (!wasSelected)
        {
            this.noProjectTeams.Add(team);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The Tasks section's "+": opens the New view page in the preview Tab, as the Tasks view's "New view" link does.</summary>
    private void NewTaskView()
    {
        const string href = "/tasks/new";
        _ = this.Tabs.Open(href, "New view");
        this.Navigation.NavigateTo(href);
    }

    /// <summary>The Rooms listed under the Team (see <see cref="roomsByTeam"/>), in a Project or not, or none before they load.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<Room> RoomsOf(TeamSummary team) =>
        this.roomsByTeam.TryGetValue(team.Name, out IReadOnlyList<Room>? teamRooms) ? teamRooms : [];

    /// <summary>The name, in the catalog's spelling, of the Project of the Team that lists <paramref name="room"/>, or <see langword="null"/> when the Room has none or its Project is gone (it is then listed at Team level, so no Room disappears).</summary>
    private static string? ProjectOf(TeamSummary team, Room room) => room.Project is { } named
        ? team.Projects.FirstOrDefault(project => string.Equals(project, named, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
        : null;

    /// <summary>The Rooms a scope lists: the Team scope's are those with no Project or whose Project is gone, a Project's are its own.</summary>
    private static IReadOnlyList<Room> ScopeRooms(TeamSummary team, IReadOnlyList<Room> allRooms, string? project) =>
        [.. allRooms.Where(room => string.Equals(ProjectOf(team, room), project, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))];

    /// <summary>The selected Project of the Team in the catalog's spelling, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team row (nothing chosen yet, or the chosen Project is gone).</summary>
    private string? SelectedProject(TeamSummary team) =>
        this.selections.TryGetValue(team.Name, out string? chosen) && chosen is not null
            ? team.Projects.FirstOrDefault(project => string.Equals(project, chosen, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
            : null;

    /// <summary>Selects the scope of the Team; choosing another one closes a New chat panel left open for the old one.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team.</param>
    /// <param name="project">The Project to select, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team row.</param>
    private void SelectScope(string team, string? project)
    {
        bool leftNoProject = this.noProjectTeams.Remove(team);
        bool changed = leftNoProject || !string.Equals(this.selections.GetValueOrDefault(team), project, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        this.selections[team] = project;
        if (changed)
        {
            this.EndNewChat();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>A click on a scope row selects it and offers its page to the Tabs, as a <c>NavTabLink</c> does; the link itself navigates.</summary>
    private void OnScopeClick(string team, string? project, string href, string title)
    {
        this.SelectScope(team, project);
        _ = this.Tabs.Open(href, title);
    }

    /// <summary>A double-click on a scope row makes its Tab permanent.</summary>
    private void KeepScopeTab(string href) => this.Tabs.KeepByKey(TabKeys.Describe(href).Key);

    /// <summary>How many Tasks of the Team are open (not Done, Cancelled, Duplicate or Rejected: the count the Tasks page shows as "open"), by Project; the Team's own are under the empty key.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team.</param>
    private Dictionary<string, int> OpenTaskCounts(string team)
    {
        Dictionary<string, int> counts = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        foreach (TaskItem task in this.Store.All)
        {
            if (task.Status.IsTerminal() || !string.Equals(task.Location.Team, team, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
            {
                continue;
            }

            string key = task.Location.Project ?? string.Empty;
            counts[key] = counts.GetValueOrDefault(key) + 1;
        }

        return counts;
    }

    /// <summary>The Room's Members from the last load, or none for a Room created since.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<User> MembersOf(Room room) =>
        this.membersByRoom.TryGetValue(room.Id, out IReadOnlyList<User>? members) ? members : [];

    /// <summary>The key of one list or folder under one Team: the Team's name followed by <paramref name="folder"/>.</summary>
    private static string FolderKey(string team, string folder) => team + folder;

    private bool IsFolderOpen(string folderKey) => !this.closedFolders.Contains(folderKey);

    private void SetFolderOpen(string folderKey, bool open) =>
        _ = open ? this.closedFolders.Remove(folderKey) : this.closedFolders.Add(folderKey);

    private void ToggleShowAllTeams() => this.showAllTeams = !this.showAllTeams;

    private void ToggleShowAllRows(string folderKey)
    {
        if (!this.showAllRows.Remove(folderKey))
        {
            this.showAllRows.Add(folderKey);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Flips the Team's state and remembers the choice; a click on the route's forced-open Team collapses it for real until the next navigation into it.</summary>
    private async Task ToggleAsync(string team)
    {
        string key = team.ToLowerInvariant();
        if (this.IsExpanded(team))
        {
            this.opened.Remove(key);
            if (string.Equals(key, this.routeTeam, StringComparison.Ordinal))
            {
                this.routeOpen = false;
            }
        }
        else
        {
            this.opened.Add(key);
        }

        // A blocked storage or a gone circuit keeps the choice for this session only.
        string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(this.opened.Order(StringComparer.Ordinal));
        _ = await BrowserStorage.TrySetAsync(this.JS, ExpandedKey, json);
    }

    /// <summary>The Team (as <see cref="roomsByTeam"/> keys it) and the Room that lists <paramref name="roomId"/>, or <see langword="null"/> when no Team lists it.</summary>
    /// <param name="roomId">The Room id of the current page, or <see langword="null"/>.</param>
    private (string Team, Room Room)? FindRoom(string? roomId)
    {
        if (roomId is null)
        {
            return null;
        }

        foreach ((string team, IReadOnlyList<Room> rooms) in this.roomsByTeam)
        {
            Room? found = rooms.FirstOrDefault(room => string.Equals(room.Id, roomId, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));
            if (found is not null)
            {
                return (team, found);
            }
        }

        return null;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Reads the Team out of <c>/teams/{Team}[/...]</c> (unescaped, lower-cased) and forces it open until the chevron
    /// collapses it, then moves that Team's selected scope to the one the address is in (see <see cref="TryReadScope"/>
    /// for a Team address, the Room's Project for a Room); any other address leaves the selection as it was.
    /// </summary>
    private void UpdateRoute()
    {
        string path = this.Navigation.ToBaseRelativePath(this.Navigation.Uri);
        int end = path.IndexOfAny(['?', '#']);
        string[] segments = (end < 0 ? path : path[..end]).Split('/');
        bool inTeam = segments.Length >= 2
            && string.Equals(segments[0], "teams", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
            && segments[1].Length > 0;
        (string Team, Room Room)? roomEntry = inTeam ? null : this.FindRoom(SidebarRows.RoomId(path));
        this.routeTeam = inTeam ? Uri.UnescapeDataString(segments[1]).ToLowerInvariant() : roomEntry?.Team.ToLowerInvariant();
        this.routeOpen = this.routeTeam is not null;
        if (this.routeTeam is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        if (roomEntry is { } entry)
        {
            string? project = this.RoomScope(entry.Team, entry.Room);
            // A Room with no Project is listed under No project as well as the Team row, so it keeps No project selected.
            if (project is not null || !this.noProjectTeams.Contains(entry.Team))
            {
                this.SelectScope(entry.Team, project);
            }

            this.OpenRoomFolders(entry.Team, project);
        }
        else if (string.Equals(segments.ElementAtOrDefault(2), NoProjectSegment, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
        {
            this.SelectScope(this.routeTeam, null);
            _ = this.noProjectTeams.Add(this.routeTeam);
        }
        else if (TryReadScope(segments, out string? scope))
        {
            this.SelectScope(this.routeTeam, scope);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Reads the scope a <c>/teams/{Team}[/...]</c> address is in: the Team page, its Tasks and its Files are the Team scope, <c>/projects/{Project}[/...]</c> is that Project's. Any other address is not in a scope.</summary>
    /// <param name="segments">The address's path, split on <c>/</c>, whose first two segments are <c>teams</c> and the Team.</param>
    /// <param name="project">The Project (unescaped), or <see langword="null"/> for the Team scope.</param>
    /// <returns><see langword="true"/> when the address is in a scope, <see langword="false"/> when the selection should be kept.</returns>
    private static bool TryReadScope(string[] segments, out string? project)
    {
        project = null;
        if (segments.Length == 2 || segments[2].Length == 0)
        {
            return true;
        }

        if (segments.Length >= 4 && string.Equals(segments[2], "projects", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
        {
            project = Uri.UnescapeDataString(segments[3]);
            return true;
        }

        return string.Equals(segments[2], "tasks", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
            || string.Equals(segments[2], "files", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
    }

    /// <summary>The Project the Team's catalog lists <paramref name="room"/> under, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team scope (no Project, or one that is gone).</summary>
    /// <param name="teamName">The Team that lists the Room, as <see cref="roomsByTeam"/> keys it.</param>
    /// <param name="room">The Room the route is on.</param>
    private string? RoomScope(string teamName, Room room)
    {
        TeamSummary? team = this.Catalog.Teams.FirstOrDefault(candidate => string.Equals(candidate.Name, teamName, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));
        return team is null ? null : ProjectOf(team, room);
    }

    /// <summary>Opens the "Needs you" and "All" folders of the scope that lists the Room, so the page the Human is on is never folded away.</summary>
    /// <param name="teamName">The Team that lists the Room.</param>
    /// <param name="project">The Room's scope: its Project, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team scope.</param>
    private void OpenRoomFolders(string teamName, string? project)
    {
        // The Team scope lists every Room, and No project the Rooms with none, so their folders open too.
        foreach (string scopeKey in new[] { project ?? string.Empty, string.Empty, ScopeFolderSuffix(null, noProject: true) }.Distinct(StringComparer.Ordinal))
        {
            this.closedFolders.Remove(FolderKey(teamName, NeedsYouFolder + scopeKey));
            this.closedFolders.Remove(FolderKey(teamName, AllFolder + scopeKey));
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Reads the Rooms again for the new catalog. The menu refs are kept: Blazor sets a ref only when it creates the menu, so
    /// clearing them would leave the rows still on screen with none. A shortcut's view whose Team has left the catalog (archived
    /// or removed) raises <see cref="TeamGone"/>, so the layout stops showing an empty view.
    /// </summary>
    private void OnCatalogChanged() => _ = RendererDispatch.RunAsync(this.InvokeAsync, async () =>
    {
        if (!this.IsTeamsView && this.Team is { } shown && this.Catalog.Find(shown) is null)
        {
            await this.TeamGone.InvokeAsync(shown);
        }

        await this.LoadRoomsAsync();
        this.StateHasChanged();
    });

    private void OnViewsChanged() => _ = RendererDispatch.Repaint(this.InvokeAsync, this.StateHasChanged);

    /// <summary>A Task written, moved or closed changes the counts, as it changes the Tasks page.</summary>
    private void OnTaskChanged(TaskChange change) => _ = RendererDispatch.Repaint(this.InvokeAsync, this.StateHasChanged);

    /// <summary>The Task files were read again (an outside edit, a new Team or Project folder), which can change every count.</summary>
    private void OnTasksReloaded() => _ = RendererDispatch.Repaint(this.InvokeAsync, this.StateHasChanged);

    private void OnTrackerChanged() => _ = RendererDispatch.RunAsync(this.InvokeAsync, () =>
    {
        this.ReadWaiting();
        this.StateHasChanged();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    });

    /// <summary>Reads the ids of the Rooms waiting on the Human (see <see cref="waitingIds"/>).</summary>
    private void ReadWaiting() =>
        this.waitingIds = new HashSet<string>(this.Tracker.Snapshot().Select(static entry => entry.RoomId), StringComparer.Ordinal);

    private void OnRoomsChanged() => _ = RendererDispatch.RunAsync(this.InvokeAsync, async () =>
    {
        await this.LoadRoomsAsync();
        this.StateHasChanged();
    });

    /// <summary>Reads the Rooms to list under every Team in the catalog (see <see cref="roomsByTeam"/>).</summary>
    private async Task LoadRoomsAsync()
    {
        int version = Interlocked.Increment(ref this.loadVersion);
        IReadOnlyList<Room> all = await this.TeamDirectory.GetRoomsAsync();
        IReadOnlyDictionary<string, IReadOnlyList<User>> members = await this.TeamDirectory.GetMembersByRoomAsync();
        if (version != Volatile.Read(ref this.loadVersion))
        {
            // A newer refresh started while this one was reading; it owns the result.
            return;
        }

        Dictionary<string, IReadOnlyList<Room>> loaded = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        foreach (TeamSummary team in this.Catalog.Teams)
        {
            List<Room> scoped = [.. all.Where(room => !room.Archived && string.Equals(room.Team, team.Name, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))];
            loaded[team.Name] =
            [
                .. scoped.Where(static room => room.IsTeamRoom),
                .. scoped.Where(static room => !room.IsTeamRoom).OrderBy(static room => room.Created),
            ];
        }

        this.ReadWaiting();
        this.membersByRoom = members;
        this.roomsByTeam.Clear();
        foreach ((string name, IReadOnlyList<Room> rooms) in loaded)
        {
            this.roomsByTeam[name] = rooms;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Opens the New chat panel for <paramref name="team"/> (and its <paramref name="project"/>), or closes it when that panel is already open.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team whose menu was used.</param>
    /// <param name="project">The Project whose scope was used, or <see langword="null"/> for the Team's own.</param>
    private void ToggleNewChat(string team, string? project = null)
    {
        bool close = this.IsNewChatOpen(team, project);
        this.newChatTeam = close ? null : team;
        this.newChatProject = close ? null : project;
    }

    /// <summary>Whether the open New chat panel is the one of <paramref name="team"/> and <paramref name="project"/>.</summary>
    private bool IsNewChatOpen(string team, string? project) =>
        string.Equals(this.newChatTeam, team, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
        && string.Equals(this.newChatProject, project, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    private void EndNewChat()
    {
        this.newChatTeam = null;
        this.newChatProject = null;
    }

    /// <summary>Shows a refusal from a Room row's Archive or Delete as a snackbar; <see langword="null"/> (a new attempt starting) shows nothing.</summary>
    /// <param name="message">The refusal's message, or <see langword="null"/>.</param>
    private void OnRoomError(string? message)
    {
        if (message is not null)
        {
            this.Snackbar.Add(message, Severity.Error, key: "teams-nav");
        }
    }

    /// <summary>How long a create action waits for the catalog to list the new Team or Project before navigating anyway.</summary>
    private static readonly TimeSpan CatalogWait = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2);

    /// <summary>Spec §6.5 Gating: a Project needs the Library or Tasks to live in, so "New project" is offered only when either is enabled.</summary>
    private bool ProjectsAllowed => this.TeamConfig.Value.Library.Enabled || this.TeamConfig.Value.Tasks.Enabled;

    /// <summary>Asks for a Project name, creates the Project's folder in <paramref name="team"/> and opens its page.</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team to start the Project in.</param>
    /// <param name="menu">The Team row's menu when its item asked, closed before the prompt opens; <see langword="null"/> for the "Start a project" row.</param>
    private async Task NewProjectAsync(string team, MudMenu? menu)
    {
        IReadOnlyList<TeamSummary> teams = this.Catalog.Teams;
        TeamSummary summary = teams.FirstOrDefault(t => string.Equals(t.Name, team, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
            ?? new TeamSummary(team, [], [], false);
        string? project = await MenuDialogs.AfterClosingAsync(menu, () => NewProjectPrompt.AskAsync(this.Dialogs, trimmed => TeamNames.ValidateProjectName(trimmed, summary), static _ => Task.FromResult<string?>(null)));
        if (project is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        await this.CreateAndOpenAsync(
            () => this.Folders.EnsureProjectIn(team, project),
            () => this.Catalog.ProjectExists(team, project),
            $"/teams/{Uri.EscapeDataString(team)}/projects/{Uri.EscapeDataString(project)}");
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Runs <paramref name="create"/>, snackbars a refusal, and otherwise navigates to <paramref name="href"/>
    /// once <paramref name="listed"/> says the catalog knows the new item (a folder created here reaches the
    /// catalog about 500 ms later, and navigating sooner flashes "There is no Team named"). The wait is driven
    /// by <see cref="ITeamCatalog.Changed"/>, subscribed BEFORE <paramref name="create"/> so no event is missed,
    /// and is bounded by <see cref="CatalogWait"/>.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task CreateAndOpenAsync(Func<LibraryResult<LibraryPath>> create, Func<bool> listed, string href)
    {
        TaskCompletionSource seen = new(TaskCreationOptions.RunContinuationsAsynchronously);
        Action onChanged = () =>
        {
            if (listed())
            {
                seen.TrySetResult();
            }
        };
        this.Catalog.Changed += onChanged;
        try
        {
            LibraryResult<LibraryPath> result = create();
            if (result.Error is { } error)
            {
                this.Snackbar.Add(error, Severity.Error, key: "teams-nav");
                return;
            }

            if (!listed())
            {
                try
                {
                    await seen.Task.WaitAsync(CatalogWait);
                }
                catch (TimeoutException)
                {
                    // Navigate anyway: the page shows its own "no such Team" text if the catalog never catches up.
                    // This timeout path has no test because it would need a real 2 s delay.
                }
            }

            this.Navigation.NavigateTo(href);
        }
        finally
        {
            this.Catalog.Changed -= onChanged;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Opens the row's own MudMenu programmatically, so a right-click reaches the same menu the "..." button does (TaskViewNav.razor's own precedent).</summary>
    /// <param name="team">The Team whose row was right-clicked.</param>
    /// <param name="e">The right-click's mouse event args, forwarded to <see cref="MudMenu.OpenMenuAsync"/>.</param>
    private async Task OnRowContextMenuAsync(string team, MouseEventArgs e)
    {
        if (this.menuRefs.TryGetValue(team, out MudMenu? menu))
        {
            await menu.OpenMenuAsync(e);
        }
    }
}
